{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>These are the generations of Aaron and Moses.</b> The sense is that they did not beget their sons and did not increase in number beyond ten months, when YHWH spoke with Moses on Mount Sinai when he went up to make atonement for the sin of the golden calf. Then the tribe of Levi was chosen, and HaShem said to Moses, Bring near the tribe of Levi, and the section of ואני הנה לקחתי (and I, behold, I have taken), and when the Tabernacle was erected HaShem said, Count the sons of Levi, and the Shekhinah was in the Tabernacle. Therefore he wrote, in the wilderness of Sinai. And so the generations of Aaron and Moses were in the wilderness of Sinai just as they were on Mount Sinai, except that Aaron's two sons were missing. Therefore I said that the Levites did not give ransom for their lives, for thus it is written, לכל העובר על הפקודים (for all who pass over to those that are counted). There are those who say that Moses did not count them before the making of the Tabernacle but only knew their count by way of prophecy, and Scripture refutes them, namely כי תשא (Exodus 30)."], :book :numbers, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 3, :notes {0 "Resolved והוא כי תשא as a citation of the Torah portion beginning Exodus 30:11, which Ibn Ezra invokes as the refutation; rendered hyper-literally without expanding the compressed argument."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:16:05.207496146Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}